      "title": "Me, you, him, her…",
      "subtitle": "Pronombres objeto",
      "goals": [
        "Usar **me, you, him, her, it, us, them** después del verbo.",
        "Usarlos después de preposiciones: *with me, for her*.",
        "No confundir pronombres sujeto y objeto."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Sujeto vs. objeto",
      "body": ["El pronombre **sujeto** va antes del verbo. El pronombre **objeto** va **después del verbo** o **después de una preposición**."],
      "table": {
        "head": ["Sujeto", "Objeto", "Ejemplo"],
        "rows": [
          ["I", "**me**", "Call **me** later."],
          ["you", "**you**", "I love **you**."],
          ["he", "**him**", "I know **him**."],
          ["she", "**her**", "Talk to **her**."],
          ["it", "**it**", "I like **it**."],
          ["we", "**us**", "Come with **us**."],
          ["they", "**them**", "I see **them** every day."]
        ]
      },
      "errors": [
        { "bad": "She loves he.", "good": "She loves **him**." },
        { "bad": "Come with we.", "good": "Come with **us**." },
        { "bad": "Me and Ana are friends.", "good": "**Ana and I** are friends.", "note": "Como sujeto se usa **I**, y por cortesía va al final." }
      ]
    },
    {
